#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:426
#: includes/class-site-health.php:225
msgid "Formats to generate"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:427
msgid "AVIF is smaller than WebP but unsupported by a few older browsers. Enable both to serve each browser its smallest option. AVIF costs a few times more CPU than WebP and runs on every image size, so if uploads slow down, turn off Convert new uploads to move the work to the background queue."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:434
#: includes/class-site-health.php:235
msgid "Convert new uploads"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:435
msgid "Convert as soon as an image is uploaded or its thumbnails are regenerated. Turn this off to convert through the background queue instead, keeping the work out of the upload request."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:441
msgid "Image sizes to convert"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:442
msgid "Leave every box unchecked to convert all sizes. If you do tick some, include the smallest and the largest: a format is withheld when an edge size is missing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:449
msgid "Maximum image dimension"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:450
msgid "Maximum width or height in pixels for new uploads supported by WordPress scaling. The unscaled upload is kept. Use 1920 for most blogs or 2560 for photography. Leave empty or use 0 to keep the WordPress default. Existing images are unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:458
msgid "Disable upload scaling"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:459
msgid "Turn off WordPress large-image scaling for new uploads. This takes precedence over Maximum image dimension."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:465
msgid "Minimum saving (%)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:466
msgid "Discard an optimized copy unless it is at least this much smaller. Small or already-compressed images often grow when re-encoded."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:475
#: includes/class-site-health.php:230
msgid "Optimized file naming"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:476
msgid "Append gives photo.jpg.webp and is the safe default. Replace gives photo.webp, which silently overwrites when photo.jpg and photo.png share a folder."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:480
msgid "Append the new extension (photo.jpg.webp) — safe"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:481
msgid "Replace the extension (photo.webp) — can collide"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:488
#: includes/class-site-health.php:236
msgid "Compress original images"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:489
msgid "Recompress served JPEG files before generating modern copies. Backups are always kept, and Restore originals reverses the changes. The unscaled WordPress original is untouched. Allow space for backups. Avoid enabling this alongside another original-image optimizer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:495
msgid "JPEG quality for originals"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:496
msgid "JPEGs with a detected quality at or below this value are kept. Changes are encoded from the first backup to avoid repeated quality loss."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:506
msgid "Compress PNG originals"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:508
msgid "Use an available local PNG tool. oxipng is lossless; pngquant reduces the palette and may change colors. Backups are kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:509
msgid "Unavailable: install oxipng (lossless, recommended) or pngquant on the server. PHP must be allowed to run it; see the wzio_png_tool_paths filter for custom locations."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:521
msgid "Resize existing originals"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:522
msgid "Apply Maximum image dimension to served main files during optimization. Requires Compress original images and a positive maximum dimension. Backups retain the previous dimensions. Existing thumbnail files and directly embedded thumbnail URLs stay unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:542
msgid "WebP quality"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:543
msgid "Between 1 and 100. The default of 82 is visually lossless for most photographs; above 90 mostly adds bytes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:552
msgid "AVIF quality"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:553
msgid "Between 1 and 100. Not comparable to WebP: AVIF at 50 looks like WebP at 82 but produces a smaller file."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:562
msgid "WebP encoder effort"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:563
msgid "Between 0 and 6. Higher spends more CPU for a smaller file at the same quality. Lower it if bulk runs time out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:565
msgid "This server encodes WebP with GD, which offers no effort control, so this setting has no effect here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:575
msgid "AVIF encoder effort"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:576
msgid "Between 0 and 6. The default is the best measured balance; above it files shrink very little for a lot more CPU. The speed this maps to depends on which encoder your server has."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:585
msgid "Strip metadata"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:586
msgid "Remove EXIF, GPS and embedded thumbnails from the copies. Color profiles are kept. This also applies to originals when optional original compression is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:592
msgid "Lossless for PNG sources"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:593
msgid "Encode the WebP copy of a PNG source with no quality loss. Right for logos and line art, much larger for photographs saved as PNG. AVIF ignores this, because a lossless AVIF is usually bigger than the PNG it came from."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:599
msgid "PNG lossy fallback quality"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:600
